To understand the driving forces behind the aggregation of both bacteria strains at the liquid-air interfaces, a thermodynamic model was developed. The total surface energy (G) of the bacterium-water-air system was calculated as a function of a dimensionless coordinate \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
